Third party parts

Forkline is built with the Godot Engine (https://godotengine.org), which is
under the MIT (Expat) license, with notices for the parts the engine
includes. The About screen shows the full engine license and every notice,
read from the engine itself.

On Android, Forkline also includes libraries that the Godot Engine's Android
build adds: the AndroidX libraries (The Android Open Source Project), the
Kotlin standard library, kotlinx.coroutines and the JetBrains Java
Annotations (JetBrains s.r.o. and contributors), the JSpecify annotations
(The JSpecify Authors) and Guava's ListenableFuture (The Guava Authors), all
under the Apache License, version 2.0, and LLVM libc++ (The LLVM Project
contributors), under the Apache License, version 2.0, with LLVM exceptions.
The About screen lists them with the license text.

Forkline uses the Outfit font, under the SIL Open Font License, version 1.1.
The license is in src/theme/fonts/OFL.txt and in the About screen.
